    "summary": "Why adjacent swings cannot share candles, and the importance of candle separation.",
    "content": "Structural swing points cannot overlap: the three candles of a swing high and the three candles of the next swing low must be separate sets.\n\n- If the three candles of a swing low overlap the three candles of the swing high before it, the low is usually not counted.\n- In Roman's picture, a bottom candle cannot count as a swing low when two of its candles overlap the candles that formed the swing high.\n- When the two sets of three candles sit next to each other, without overlap, it is better and both can count as a swing high and a swing low.\n- Roman says sometimes they can overlap, but he will show those special cases later.",
