    "content": "The aim of the walkthrough is not to find a trade yet. It is to find the tradable zone, which is the range between the latest structural swing high and swing low.\n\nRoman uses the replay mode on a 4-hour chart that is in a bearish structure.\n\n### Step 1: Choose a Good Starting Point\nYou can start anywhere, but make sure the start is correct. Go back a little and find a place where you can see a break of structure, where earlier swings were clearly broken. Do not start from unimportant points.\n\n### Step 2: Understand the Current Range\nPrice breaks below the previous swing low. Now you cannot call any swing high in the current area. Price has to get out of the current range first.\n- Until then, any high inside the range is only an internal high.\n- At this moment you have one high and one low. This is the structure you work with. It is a bearish structure, and you trade only inside this area.\n- You cannot identify new swings inside the area until price goes above or below it.",
