    "content": "Until price breaks beyond the area you cannot mark new swings, even though it is tempting.\n\nRoman checks the 4H chart and notes a short would have worked here. Price was in a bearish structure, so it kept falling. There was upward momentum, but nothing big, and it did not hold. The Fibonacci tool shows the best entry range for shorts. Fibonacci is taught in a later stream.\n\n### Wick vs Body Close: Sweep or Break?\n- Look at a swing high. If price breaks it with only a weak close (a wick), it is just a liquidity sweep. You do not count it as a break of structure.\n- If a candle closes with its body beyond the swing, the swing is broken. That is a real break.",
