        "content": "1. A swing is three candles. Only the extreme wick points count, not the bodies.\n2. Structural swings cannot overlap, and you want something between them.\n3. A swing is valid only after confirmation: a close beyond the red line.\n4. Inside the range, mark nothing. Wait for a break of the range.\n5. A wick beyond a level is a sweep. A body close beyond it is a break.\n6. After a break, take the extreme point between the two swings as the new swing.\n7. Do not trade against the higher time frame without care.\n8. A small range gives more trades. A large range gives few.\n9. Practise with replay, with no trades."
